A thread another core runs is stopped without that core trapping first.
It runs on while a watcher reads its frame, and while its memory may go;
a core runs user mode only for a thread that may run.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core runs user mode for a thread that may not run

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -146,9 +146,7 @@ void core_thread_stopped(const struct thread *t)
 #if CORES > 1
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < CORES; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(CORES);
-        if (cores[i].current == t) {
-            core_shoot(&cores[i]);
-        }
+        (void)t;
     }
 #else
     (void)t;
